+# Build menu hitches
+
+## Problem
+
+Every tab switch destroyed the current page and built the new one from scratch (Vide `switch`).
+The Shapes page is about 450 instances (≈40 ms frame) and Colors about 370 (≈30 ms). Closing the
+menu also destroyed the whole menu (`show(isMenuOpen, …)`), so every open rebuilt the panel plus
+whichever page was last selected.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Pages are built once and kept** (`BuildMenu.luau`). The menu tracks which tabs have been
+  visited and renders them with `Vide.values`. A page is built the first time you visit its tab;
+  after that, switching tabs only flips each page's `Visible`.
+- **The menu is built once and kept** (`Main.client.luau`). The menu now mounts on the first open
+  (`hasMenuOpened`, which never goes back to false) instead of following `isMenuOpen`. Opening
+  and closing only drive `Present`, which runs the same slide spring as before.
+- **The closed panel is hidden.** Once the slide-out spring settles, the panel's `Visible` turns
+  off, so the off-screen menu does no rendering or layout work.
+- **The rainbow swatch only runs while you can see it.** Its Heartbeat connection is only active
+  while the Colors tab is selected and the menu is open. Before, the page was destroyed when
+  hidden; now it is kept, so without this it would keep updating every frame.
+- **Looks the same.** The first open still slides in, closing still slides out, and Shapes/Colors
+  still start scrolled to the top each time they're shown, like when they were rebuilt.
+
+Still expected: one spike the first time you open the menu, and one the first time you visit each
+of Colors and Shapes in a session. Nothing is built ahead of time.
+
+## How to check in Studio
+
+1. Play Solo, then open the MicroProfiler (Ctrl+F6). Pause it (Ctrl+P) when you want to inspect
+   frames.
+2. Open the menu (M) and visit Blocks, Colors and Shapes once each. You should see the same
+   one-time spikes as before. These are the first builds.
+3. Now switch between the tabs several times, and close and reopen the menu while it is on Shapes
+   and on Colors. Those frames should now be close to your normal ~8 ms, with no 30–40 ms spikes.
+4. To confirm nothing is being rebuilt: in the Explorer, expand
+   `Players > <you> > PlayerGui > BuildMenuGui > BuildMenu > Page`. After you've visited all three
+   tabs it has three children (`Blocks`, `Colors`, `Shapes`). Switching tabs only toggles their
+   `Visible`, and the instances stay the same (they don't flash or get re-added in the Explorer).
+   Closing the menu leaves `BuildMenu` in place with `Visible = false`.
+5. Optional: run `print(#game.Players.LocalPlayer.PlayerGui.BuildMenuGui:GetDescendants())` in
+   the command bar (set to client) before and after switching tabs. The count should stay the same.
